    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Vocabulary</span> built around culture, social institutions and ceremonies helps you read and write confidently about Nigerian and African society — a favourite source of comprehension passages, essay topics, and oral literature texts in WAEC/NECO English.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Words Associated with Ceremonies</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Ceremonies mark important stages and events in community life. Key vocabulary includes:</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Naming ceremony</td><td>Ritual event at which a new baby is officially given a name</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Chieftaincy</td><td>The rank, office or title of a traditional chief</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Title-taking</td><td>The formal process of being conferred with a traditional title</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Installation</td><td>The formal ceremony of putting a person into a traditional office</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Festival</td><td>A day or period of celebration, usually religious or cultural</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ritual</td><td>A series of actions performed according to a prescribed order, often religious</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Words Associated with Institutions and Social Norms</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">These words describe how society is organised and how people are expected to behave:</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Social norm</td><td>An accepted standard of behaviour within a group</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Morality</td><td>Principles concerning right and wrong behaviour</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Custom</td><td>A traditional practice passed down within a community</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Social class</td><td>A division of society based on status, wealth, or occupation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Family life</td><td>The pattern of relationships and roles within a household</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Words Related to African Arts, Sculpture and Age Groups</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Traditional societies organise life around <span class=\"learn-keyword\">age groups</span> (also called age-grades) and express identity through <span class=\"learn-keyword\">sculpture</span> (carved figures in wood, stone or bronze) and oral <span class=\"learn-keyword\">lyrics</span> (words of songs, chants, or praise poetry). An <em>age group</em> is a set of people born within the same years who move through life stages — and their duties — together, such as clearing farmland or defending the village.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Vocabulary questions often test the word that best fits a sentence about culture. Learn each word's exact meaning rather than a vague impression — \"chieftaincy\" is a rank/office, while \"installation\" is the ceremony of being placed into that office.\n</div>\n",
