    "topic": "Comprehension – Silent Reading on Topical Issues",
    "topicCode": "SS3-ENG-05",
    "module": "Comprehension",
    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Silent reading comprehension</span> tests your ability to read a passage independently, understand its meaning, and answer questions of varying difficulty — including vocabulary-in-context questions. WAEC passages often focus on topical social issues.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Common Topical Issues in WAEC Passages</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Passages frequently discuss: population explosion, youth unemployment, youth restiveness, being your brother's keeper, examination malpractice, and corruption. Familiarity with these themes helps you anticipate vocabulary and arguments.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Steps for Effective Silent Reading</h3>\n<ol class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Skim the passage once quickly to get the general idea (the \"gist\")</li>\n  <li>Read the questions before reading the passage closely, so you know what to look for</li>\n  <li>Read carefully a second time, underlining or noting key points</li>\n  <li>Answer literal questions (facts stated directly) using exact information from the text</li>\n  <li>Answer inferential questions (meaning implied but not directly stated) using reasoning based on the text</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Types of Comprehension Questions</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Literal</td><td>Answer is directly stated in the passage</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inferential</td><td>Answer must be worked out from clues in the passage</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Vocabulary-in-context</td><td>Asks the meaning of a word as used in the passage, which may differ from its dictionary meaning</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Main idea</td><td>Asks for the central point or theme of a paragraph or the whole passage</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Answering Vocabulary-in-Context Questions</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Never rely only on the word's usual dictionary meaning. Instead, look at how the word is used in the surrounding sentence — the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">context</span> — since many words have multiple meanings.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Always answer comprehension questions using your own words as much as possible, while staying accurate to what the passage says. Copying long sentences directly from the passage without adapting them can lose marks.\n</div>\n",
