    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Listening comprehension</span> tests your ability to follow spoken English — speeches, radio broadcasts, and recorded talks — and extract main ideas accurately, without the benefit of re-reading a printed text.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Why Listening Skills Matter</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Unlike reading, listening happens in real time — you cannot pause a live speaker. Strong listening skills help you follow lectures, announcements, news broadcasts, and instructions accurately the first time.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Identifying Main Ideas While Listening</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Listen for signal words that introduce main points: \"firstly\", \"importantly\", \"in conclusion\"</li>\n  <li>Pay attention to repeated ideas — speakers often repeat their most important points</li>\n  <li>Note changes in the speaker's tone or pace, which often signal emphasis</li>\n  <li>Distinguish the main idea from supporting details and examples</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Note-Taking Techniques</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Abbreviations</td><td>Use short forms (e.g., \"govt\" for government, \"&\" for and) to write faster</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Keywords only</td><td>Write only important words, not full sentences</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Numbering</td><td>Number points as the speaker presents them, to preserve order</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Symbols</td><td>Use arrows, plus/minus signs to show cause-effect or increase-decrease</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Radio Broadcasts</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Radio broadcasts often follow a structured format: headline/introduction, main content, and a closing summary. Listening for this structure helps you anticipate what type of information (who, what, where, when) is coming next.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> In a listening exercise, do not try to write down every word. Focus on capturing main ideas and key facts using short notes, then reconstruct full sentences afterward if required.\n</div>\n",
