    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This final topic develops listening skills applied specifically to <span class=\"learn-keyword\">dramatic presentations</span> — plays performed or read aloud — focusing on identifying themes and following storylines by ear.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. What is a Dramatic Presentation?</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A dramatic presentation is a performed or read-aloud version of a play, involving dialogue between characters, stage directions, and dramatic tension. Unlike a novel, drama relies heavily on spoken dialogue and action to convey the story.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Identifying Theme While Listening</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">theme</span> is the central message or underlying idea of a literary work — such as \"the corrupting influence of power\" or \"the value of loyalty.\" While listening to a drama, ask: What lesson or idea does this play seem to be exploring through its characters' choices and conflicts?</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Following Storyline (Plot) by Ear</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">storyline</span> (plot) is the sequence of events in the drama. To follow it while listening, track:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Who the main characters are, identified by their distinct voices or names used in dialogue</li>\n  <li>The central conflict or problem driving the action</li>\n  <li>Key turning points where the situation changes significantly</li>\n  <li>How the conflict is resolved by the end</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Distinguishing Theme from Plot</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Plot</th><th>Theme</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>What happens in the story (events, sequence)</td><td>What the story means (the underlying message)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Specific to that one story</td><td>Often universal, applying beyond the specific story</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When asked for the \"theme\" of a drama, avoid simply retelling the plot. State the underlying message or lesson in one or two general sentences, e.g., \"greed leads to one's downfall,\" rather than summarising events.\n</div>\n",
